Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-bandix: phone layout of the status page

On screens up to 768 px the status page showed the device list as
cards with every value on its own line, ignored the display mode
("Detailed Mode" was forced to "Simple Mode" there) and left about
270 of 390 px for the content because of the nested section paddings.
The query panels of the ranking and the timeline took most of a screen
each, and the timeline canvas was drawn 300 px high in a 250 px box, so
its time labels covered the totals under it.

On narrow screens now:

- the sections use smaller paddings; LAN, WAN and Total are three
  columns;
- the legend of the realtime chart goes under its title, the device and
  type selects are in one row;
- the device list has Period, Display mode and a Sort select (online
  status, WAN or LAN rate or volume; the desktop table keeps sorting by
  its headers and does not show this select);
- a device card shows the name (or the address), the address and the
  connection type, and a grid with WAN and LAN: the rate up and down
  with the volume for the period under it. Detailed mode adds IPv4, MAC,
  LAN IPv6 and the last seen time. Offline devices are dimmed;
- date fields go in two columns, the network type and the Query/Reset
  buttons in their own rows, the period presets in two columns;
- a ranking item keeps the rank, the name and the totals in one block;
- the timeline filters are in one row, the canvas takes the height of
  its box and narrower margins, the totals are three columns.

The timeline left margin now fits the widest Y label, not only the top
and zero ones (an intermediate label was cut on narrow screens); the
hover check uses the margins the chart was drawn with. The desktop
layout (wider than 768 px) does not change.

New strings are translated to Russian.

